        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1. Overview</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;Fake Dream&quot; is a survival action horror game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>2. Story</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You're visiting a town for work.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tired and remorseful, you fall asleep while waiting for a train at the station.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When you wake up, you find yourself in a world that seems real, but somehow different.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As you battle the inhabitants of this other world, you must confront your own regrets and true nature.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>3. Supported Languages</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Supports 12 languages: Japanese, English, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Korean, Russian, German, French, Portuguese, Spanish, Italian, and Turkish.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>4. Controls</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Supports both mouse and keyboard and gamepad.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>5. Tutorial</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Conveniently designed with on-screen control instructions.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>6. Playtime</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Estimated for a first-time player: approximately 5-6 hours.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>7. Continue</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you experience a game over, you can continue from the previous scene.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>8. Difficulty</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are four difficulty levels: Easy, Normal, Hard, and Nightmare.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Easy: Enemy attack power and health are 0.5 times that of normal.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Normal: Standard.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Hard: Enemy attack power and health are 1.5 times that of normal.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Nightmare: Enemy attack power and health are 2 times that of normal. (Unlocked after clearing Hard mode.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>9. Carryover</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game allows you to continue playing with your previous data, carrying over your money, HP, equipment, number of slots, etc.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Difficulty levels can also be changed. You can start on a lower difficulty level and then challenge a higher difficulty level.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>10. Weapons</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Weapons are broadly divided into three types: firearms, melee weapons, and thrown weapons.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are multiple types of firearms and melee weapons.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Firearms can be improved in terms of attack power, rate of fire, range (the degree of power falloff over distance), critical chance, and maximum ammo capacity.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Melee weapons can be used for both attack and defense. However, defense requires remaining durability (attacks are possible even if durability is depleted).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>11. Armor</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Reduces damage taken and prevents status ailments. Armor loses its effectiveness when durability is depleted.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>12. Shop</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ammunition, recovery items, etc. can be purchased using the in-game currency, &quot;Karma.&quot;</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Firearms can be upgraded and melee weapons and armor can be repaired in the same way.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Karma accumulates automatically when enemies are defeated. You can also earn &quot;Karma&quot; by selling crystals scattered throughout the stage.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>13. Enemies</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Use a variety of weapons.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In addition to humanoid enemies, there are also animal and plant-type enemies.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In addition to enemies that attack normally, various types of enemies will appear, including the following:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enemies that inflict status ailments</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enemies whose bodies can separate</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Armored enemies</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enemies that are only effective against specific parts</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Invulnerable enemies</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>14. Body Part Destruction</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Some enemies' heads and limbs can be destroyed.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>15. Stage</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The stage is fairly large, centered around a city.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The buildings you can enter are also fairly large.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>16. Puzzle Solving</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In addition to using key items, you'll also turn safe dials, align puzzle pieces, and rotate panels.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>17. Stealth</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >During the game, there are enemies that are invincible and can launch instant-death attacks.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You'll need to hide to avoid being detected and obtain items needed to escape.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>18. Achievements</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A total of 36 are available.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>19. Clear Time Record</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can record your top 10 clear times for each difficulty level. Aim for a faster clear time.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>20. Movies</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Several are available.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1. Overview</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;Fake Dream&quot; is a survival action horror game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>2. Story</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You're visiting a town for work.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tired and remorseful, you fall asleep while waiting for a train at the station.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When you wake up, you find yourself in a world that seems real, but somehow different.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As you battle the inhabitants of this other world, you must confront your own regrets and true nature.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>3. Supported Languages</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Supports 12 languages: Japanese, English, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Korean, Russian, German, French, Portuguese, Spanish, Italian, and Turkish.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>4. Controls</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Supports both mouse and keyboard and gamepad.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>5. Tutorial</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Conveniently designed with on-screen control instructions.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>6. Playtime</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Estimated for a first-time player: approximately 5-6 hours.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>7. Continue</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you experience a game over, you can continue from the previous scene.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>8. Difficulty</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are four difficulty levels: Easy, Normal, Hard, and Nightmare.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Easy: Enemy attack power and health are 0.5 times that of normal.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Normal: Standard.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Hard: Enemy attack power and health are 1.5 times that of normal.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Nightmare: Enemy attack power and health are 2 times that of normal. (Unlocked after clearing Hard mode.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>9. Carryover</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game allows you to continue playing with your previous data, carrying over your money, HP, equipment, number of slots, etc.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Difficulty levels can also be changed. You can start on a lower difficulty level and then challenge a higher difficulty level.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>10. Weapons</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Weapons are broadly divided into three types: firearms, melee weapons, and thrown weapons.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are multiple types of firearms and melee weapons.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Firearms can be improved in terms of attack power, rate of fire, range (the degree of power falloff over distance), critical chance, and maximum ammo capacity.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Melee weapons can be used for both attack and defense. However, defense requires remaining durability (attacks are possible even if durability is depleted).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>11. Armor</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Reduces damage taken and prevents status ailments. Armor loses its effectiveness when durability is depleted.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>12. Shop</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ammunition, recovery items, etc. can be purchased using the in-game currency, &quot;Karma.&quot;</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Firearms can be upgraded and melee weapons and armor can be repaired in the same way.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Karma accumulates automatically when enemies are defeated. You can also earn &quot;Karma&quot; by selling crystals scattered throughout the stage.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>13. Enemies</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Use a variety of weapons.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In addition to humanoid enemies, there are also animal and plant-type enemies.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In addition to enemies that attack normally, various types of enemies will appear, including the following:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enemies that inflict status ailments</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enemies whose bodies can separate</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Armored enemies</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enemies that are only effective against specific parts</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Invulnerable enemies</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>14. Body Part Destruction</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Some enemies' heads and limbs can be destroyed.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>15. Stage</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The stage is fairly large, centered around a city.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The buildings you can enter are also fairly large.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>16. Puzzle Solving</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In addition to using key items, you'll also turn safe dials, align puzzle pieces, and rotate panels.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>17. Stealth</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >During the game, there are enemies that are invincible and can launch instant-death attacks.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You'll need to hide to avoid being detected and obtain items needed to escape.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>18. Achievements</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A total of 36 are available.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>19. Clear Time Record</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can record your top 10 clear times for each difficulty level. Aim for a faster clear time.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>20. Movies</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Several are available.</p>",
